# Local sidecars

The desktop shell runs the API and model planes as loopback sidecars so the
app works offline and local models stay out of the UI process.

Phase 3 wires this directory:

- build the API as a PyInstaller one-dir bundle or a Rust binary;
- build the model service as a PyInstaller one-dir bundle;
- start each on `127.0.0.1` with port 0 and a per-session token;
- health-check, restart on crash, and kill on app exit;
- keep models in a separate download/update channel.

The UI still calls `http://127.0.0.1:<port>`; nothing runs in the renderer.
